---
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What The Hydration Code actually collects: cookie-less analytics via Plausible, and an email address only if you submit one to the newsletter."
>
  <p>
    This policy describes what actually happens on this site — not a generic template. If a data
    practice isn't listed here, we don't do it.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use <a href="https://plausible.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible
    Analytics</a> to understand which pages get read. Plausible does not use cookies, does not
    fingerprint your device, and does not track you across other websites. It reports aggregate,
    anonymized numbers — page views and referral sources — and cannot identify you individually. Because
    no cookies or personal identifiers are involved, no cookie consent banner is required or shown.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also track a small number of custom events (an affiliate link click, a newsletter signup, which
    research pillar a link belongs to) through the same Plausible integration, for the same aggregate
    purpose: understanding what's useful, not building a profile of any individual reader.
  </p>

  <h2>Newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit your email address to the newsletter form, that address is sent to our email
    delivery provider for the sole purpose of sending you the newsletter. We do not sell, rent, or
    otherwise share that address with any third party. Every email includes an unsubscribe link, and
    unsubscribing removes you immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Clicking a product link on this site (routed through a <code>/go/</code> redirect) takes you to a
    retailer — currently Amazon — whose own privacy policy governs whatever happens on their site. We
    don't see or store any information about what you do after you leave. See the <a
    href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> for how these links work.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No user accounts, logins, or profiles.</li>
    <li>No browser storage APIs — no localStorage, no sessionStorage, no tracking cookies.</li>
    <li>No advertising networks, retargeting pixels, or third-party trackers of any kind beyond Plausible.</li>
    <li>No selling or sharing of any data we collect.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If what this site actually collects changes, this page will be updated to match — not the other
    way around.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:hello@thehydrationcode.com">hello@thehydrationcode.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
